# Local configuration for PRE-RELEASE publishing (see docs/features/prerelease.md).
#
#   cp tools/prerelease/registry.env.example tools/prerelease/registry.env
#
# Copy to `registry.env` — which is gitignored — and fill in the two values that are not
# committed. Every value can also come from an environment variable of the same name,
# which is what a second checkout or a machine with no config should use.
#
# Nothing here is committed or defaulted, and the address is deliberately in that set:
#   MO_REGISTRY_BASE   the registry's address — infrastructure belonging to whoever runs
#                      it. This repository is public and a committed default would carry
#                      one operator's hostname into every reader and every fork.
#   MO_REGISTRY_OWNER  an account name; likewise not named here.
#   MO_REGISTRY_TOKEN  a credential. Never commit it, never paste it into a consumer.
#
# READS ARE ANONYMOUS. Consuming a pre-release needs the base URL and the owner — no
# account, no token. Only PUBLISHING needs the token.
#
# No registry yet? `docker compose -f tools/prerelease/docker-compose.yml up -d` stands
# one up, and tools/prerelease/bootstrap.sh fills in the rest.

# Base URL, no trailing slash. Required — the tooling refuses rather than guessing.
MO_REGISTRY_BASE=https://<registry-host>

# The registry account/organisation that owns the published packages.
MO_REGISTRY_OWNER=<owner>

# A token with write:package + read:package scope. PUBLISHING ONLY.
MO_REGISTRY_TOKEN=<token>

# The registry account password. Only tools/prerelease/bootstrap.sh uses it (and generates
# one when absent); publishing authenticates with the token, never the password.
#MO_REGISTRY_PASS=
